body:
**[comments] Rule 2, restates identifiers: shorten**

"Contiguous ... head_size bf16 values" restates const_view<bf16, ..., seq<Cols>, sseq<1>>, and "the caller's alignment and DMA flags travel with the row" restates the Aligned and Dma template parameters. "For page::set_k_row / page::get_k_row" is caller context; the aliases are also the parameter types of store_row and load_row in this file. The fact that stays is that the Aligned flag, which defaults to VIEW_ALIGNED_TRUE, is not a requirement.

Proposed:
```cpp
// Transfer rows: one token's values in dimension order, not packed storage.
// Aligned is not a precondition (unlike the packed V rows): store_row and load_row
// use unaligned loads and stores.
```

Line-to-code mapping (Rule 4):
line 1 (one token's values in order, not packed) -> seq<Cols>, sseq<1> of the alias; line 2 (Aligned is not a precondition) -> bool Aligned = VIEW_ALIGNED_TRUE; line 3 (unaligned loads and stores) -> same default, explained by _mm512_loadu_si512 / _mm512_storeu_si512 in store_row and load_row
